FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
SOFTWARE.

## The LDraw data: CC BY, and not ours to relicense

The MIT grant above does **not** cover these paths:

| Path | What it is | Licence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `public/models/*.mpd` | Packed models, each with the part files it uses inlined | CC BY 2.0 and CC BY 4.0, per block |
| `public/parts/palette.mpd` | The free-build parts, same inlining | CC BY 2.0 and CC BY 4.0, per block |
| `public/ldraw/LDConfig.ldr` | LDraw.org's colour table | CC BY 2.0 and CC BY 4.0 |
| `public/omr-index.json` | Set numbers, names, themes and years scraped from the OMR set list | Facts about published sets; see below |

Part geometry and colour definitions come from the LDraw Parts Library,
<https://library.ldraw.org/>, © the LDraw.org contributors named in each file's
`0 Author:` line, under [CC BY 2.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/)
and [CC BY 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Which one applies
is per part, and stated in that part's own `0 !LICENSE` line: parts submitted or
edited on or after 2023-03-05 are CC BY 4.0, older ones are CC BY 2.0 or both.
`CCAL version 2.0`, the older spelling, means CC BY 2.0. `CAreadme.txt` in the
library is the authority on all of this.

Two of the packed models are official sets from the [LDraw Official Model
Repository](https://library.ldraw.org/omr/sets), redistributed under the CCAL
licence line each carries, and credited to the person who built them:

- `public/models/galaxy-explorer.mpd` — 928 Galaxy Explorer, by Willy Tschager
  [Holly-Wood]
- `public/models/saturn-v.mpd` — 21309 NASA Apollo Saturn V, by Jaco van der
  Molen [Jaco]

**These files are modified.** Packing inlines every part file a model references
and normalises its name to the key `LDrawLoader` looks it up by. No geometry is
altered and no header is dropped, so each block keeps the `0 Author:` and
`0 !LICENSE` lines it shipped with. Each packed file states this in its own
header. Reusing them means carrying that attribution onward; the licence is the
part authors' to enforce, not this project's to waive.

`public/omr-index.json` holds only the set number, name, theme and year of
published sets, which are facts rather than creative expression. It is
regenerated by `pnpm ldraw:index` and is a convenience for the search box, not a
copy of the OMR's models.

## Third-party software

Dependency licences and copyright notices are in [NOTICES.md](NOTICES.md),
generated from the installed production tree by `pnpm notices`.

